r("Jason Asano",["Jason","Jason Asano","Asano","the Hegemon","Mr Asano","John Miller","System Administrator"],
"""Jason Asano is the series' protagonist: an Australian from the coastal town of Casselton Beach who was a retail assistant manager and political-science dropout when, at twenty-three, a failed summoning by the Builder cultist Landemere Vane dragged him across the cosmos to Pallimustus. The transit destroyed his body; his soul rebuilt one like a familiar's, leaving him hairless and with no heart or lungs to speak of. He is an irreverent, rambling joker who quotes films and television, deflects with humour, and hides self-doubt and a strong moral conscience behind a deliberately villainous flair. His father is Ken (a landscape architect), his mother Cheryl, his sister Erika, his brother Kaito (who married Jason's first love, Amy), his niece Emi, and his uncles Hiro and Shiro.

His build is that of an affliction specialist. His four essences are Dark, Blood and Sin, which combine into the Doom confluence; his attributes are Power (Blood), Speed (Dark), Spirit (Doom) and Recovery (Sin). He fights with Way of the Reaper martial arts, a soul-bound sword (Dread Salvation, later Hegemon's Will) and shadow arms, and is aided by three familiars: Shade, Colin and Gordon. He can't be tracked or identified by magic. He reaches iron in Book 1, bronze in Book 3, silver in Book 5 and gold in Book 12, dying and returning several times along the way.

Over the series he becomes an astral king, repairs the Cosmic Throne by sitting on it, and becomes the administrator of the System that every essence-user in the cosmos now sees. In 2038 (Book 13) he is a gold-rank prime avatar of an astral nexus, roughly forty-four years old, and has not been fully human for two decades. At the end of Book 13 his consciousness is bound into that avatar by Umber while Knowledge prepares to cross the bridge to Earth.""",
["Jason Asano"])
